# New radio host lines (Shelly #386892). Script is Savi's.
RALPH = [
("Late Shift", "Evening, wanderers. It's late, or early, or neither. Down here the clock just shrugs. Grab an almond water, put your feet up. Radio Backrooms has you."),
("Survival 101: Shoes", "Survival 101. Tip number twelve: take care of your shoes. Carpet looks soft, but a few thousand miles of it will eat a sole alive. Your feet are your ride home."),
("Survival 101: Doors", "Survival 101. Tip number thirteen: if a door's been closed a long time, knock first. Not because anybody answers. Because sometimes they do."),
("Survival 101: Light", "Tip number fourteen: carry a light. Smilers hate it, Hounds don't love it, and you'll want to see who's sharing the hallway."),
("Mail Bag", "Got a letter in the mail bag. Well, a napkin. It says: Ralph, how do I get out? Friend, I'll tell you as soon as I find out. Keep the napkins coming."),
("Level of the Day: Level 1", "Level of the day, Level One. Concrete, puddles, crates full of supplies, and the good folks at M.E.G. Base Alpha. If you're new, that's where you want to be. Tell 'em Ralph sent you. They won't know who that is."),
("Level of the Day: The Poolrooms", "Level of the day, Level Thirty-Seven, the Poolrooms. Warm water, white tile, nobody around. Prettiest place you'll ever feel completely alone in. Bring a towel."),
("Level of the Day: Level 4", "Level of the day, Level Four. Empty offices, water coolers that actually work. Feels like Monday morning with nobody to boss you around. Paradise, almost."),
("Weather", "Weather report. Level Zero: humid, buzzing, seventy two degrees forever. Level Six: dark. Level Eleven: lovely, actually. Go see Level Eleven."),
("Almond Water Moment", "This is your almond water moment. Stop. Take a sip. Breathe. You're still here, and that counts for something. Okay. Back to it."),
("Ralph's Story", "People ask how I ended up behind a mic. I found this room, found this board, flipped one switch, and the light came on. Been talking ever since. Seemed rude to stop."),
("Shout Out", "Shout out to whoever left a full can of beans by the stairwell on Level Two. You're a saint. I ate them. Sorry to the next guy."),
("Sprinkles Report", "Word is Sprinkles over on Join Us Radio is throwing another party. Friendly reminder from your pal Ralph: do not RSVP. Do not bring cake. Do not go."),
("Ole'hba Report", "Our friend Ole'hba over on eight-eight-point-eight says hello. Well, he said something. I'm choosing to hear hello. Keep your lights on, folks."),
("Song Intro: Slow One", "Here's a slow one. For anybody walking a long hallway right now, wondering if it ever ends. It does. Then there's another one. But this song helps."),
("Song Intro: Swing", "Let's pick it up a little. Something with some swing. Dance if you want. Nobody's watching. Well. Probably nobody."),
("Late Night Thoughts", "You ever notice the hum sounds like a note? I think it's a B flat. Been trying to harmonize with it for years. Might be the reason I'm still single."),
("Advice Line", "Advice line. Caller asks: Ralph, the walls keep moving. What do I do? Honestly? Move with them. Pick a wall, make friends. Walls are good listeners."),
("Gratitude", "I know this place is hard. But you found a radio, and you found me, and that's two good things. Count those. I'm counting you."),
("Station ID 2", "You're tuned to Radio Backrooms, twenty-nine point four AM. Coming to you live from somewhere warm, dry, and suspiciously yellow."),
("Sign Off Bit", "That's about all the talking I've got for now. Stay hydrated, stay lit, and if something smiles at you in the dark, do not smile back. Ralph out. Well, not out. Just quiet."),
("Cashew Water PSA", "Public service announcement. Cashew water is not almond water. I don't care how thirsty you are. It's not the same. It's never the same. Please."),
]
SPRINKLES = [
("Hiii", "[giggles] Hiiii! It's Sprinkles! You're listening to Join Us! Radio, the PARTY station! [gasps] Are you at a party right now? You should be!"),
("MEG Clipboard", "Okay so like, M.E.G. came to my party and they brought a CLIPBOARD. [gasps] Who brings a clipboard to a party?! I put frosting on it. They didn't laugh."),
("Counting", "I tried counting how many friends I have. I got to like... seven? And then I forgot what comes after seven. [giggles] So I started over! Party!"),
("Cake", "Cake is my favorite food. And my favorite color. And my favorite word. Cake. [laughs] Cake cake cake. Wait, what were we talking about?"),
("MEG Stinks", "[groans] M.E.G. keeps putting signs up that say DO NOT ENTER. Rude! I entered anyway. I always enter. [giggles] That's what doors are FOR, silly."),
("Balloon Facts", "Fun fact! Balloons are full of air. And air is free. So balloons are free! [gasps] So everybody gets a balloon! Except M.E.G. They get a sad balloon."),
("Lost Again", "I got lost again. [giggles] It's okay, every room looks like a party room if you squint. And if you scream. [screams happily] See? Party!"),
("Invitation", "You're invited! To the party! Where? [pause] Here! When? Now! Forever! [giggles] You can't leave. I mean you CAN. But why would you? Hee hee."),
("MEG Report", "Breaking news! M.E.G. says Partygoers are, quote, extremely dangerous. [gasps] That's so mean! I'm only a little dangerous! Like, a sprinkle of dangerous!"),
("Shapes", "Today I learned shapes! Circle. Circle. [pause] Also circle. [giggles] I think everything's a circle if you hug it hard enough."),
("Dance Break", "Dance break! Everybody dance! [giggles] Spin, spin, spin, oops I fell down. [laughs] That counts! That counts as dancing!"),
("Smile", "Smile! No not like that. BIGGER. [giggles] Biiigger. Show me ALL your teeth. Yay! Now you look like a Partygoer! We're twins!"),
("MEG Party", "I sent M.E.G. a party invite and they sent back a, um, cease and... desist? [gasps] I don't know what that is but it sounds like a dance! I'm gonna cease and desist all night!"),
("Phone Call", "We have a caller! Hello? [pause] Hello? [giggles] They hung up. They're shy. That's okay, I'll find them later. I always find them."),
("Snacks", "Snack time! I made cupcakes. They're made of, um, cup. And cake. [giggles] Don't ask what's in the frosting. It's a surprise!"),
("Big Words", "M.E.G. says I have no impulse control. [pause] What's an impulse? Is it a snack? [gasps] Can I have one? I want ALL the impulses!"),
("Sad Moment", "Sometimes I get sad when the party ends. [sniffles] But then I remember... it never ends! [giggles] Never ever ever! Yaaay!"),
("Game Show", "Let's play a game! I say a word, you say party. Ready? Cake! [pause] You were supposed to say party. [giggles] Okay you lose. Losers have to stay. Forever."),
("MEG Agent", "A M.E.G. agent ran away from me today. He was SO fast. [laughs] I think he wanted to play tag! Tag, you're it! You're it forever!"),
("Music Intro", "Okay, here's a song! It's my favorite. It's every song's my favorite. [giggles] Turn it up! Louder! LOUDER! Okay that's loud enough. No it isn't. LOUDER!"),
("Station ID 2", "This is Join Us! Radio! [party horn] Smiley face FM! Tell your friends! Bring your friends! [giggles] Bring ALL of your friends. We have room."),
("Goodnight", "It's bedtime for some people. [gasps] Not for me! I don't sleep! [giggles] Sweet dreams! Don't let M.E.G. bite! They don't bite. I do. [giggles] Kidding!"),
]
OLEHBA = [
("The Story, Again", "[clears throat] So. As I was saying. Before I came to the basement, I was a simple shadow on Level Zero, until one day... [long pause] Hold on. I have to sneeze. [sneezes] Where was I. Doesn't matter."),
("Fart", "Welcome back to eight bit hits. Ole'hba here, the most terrifying voice in the dark. [farts loudly into the mic] [long silence] ...That was the static. The static did that."),
("Cashew Water", "Some fool left a bottle of cashew water in my studio. Let's see what the humans drink. [gulps] [coughs violently] [gags] [coughing] WHAT IS THAT. [chewing loudly] Okay. Okay. I'm eating a cracker. I'm fine."),
("Threat", "I can see you listening. Yes. You. With the radio. [whispers] Turn the light off. Turn it off. I just want to talk. [chuckles darkly] Mostly talk."),
("Wikidot Lore: Smilers", "The humans wrote about my kind on their little website. Entity three. Smilers. They say if you see us, don't look away and back away slowly. [scoffs] Lies. Run. Running is funnier."),
("The Story, Part Two", "Okay. The story. It was dark, darker than usual, and I heard a sound. A beautiful sound. It was... [burps] Excuse me. It was that. No, it wasn't that. Forget it."),
("Lore: Level 6", "Level Six. Lights Out. My vacation home. [chuckles] Pitch black, cool air, humans tripping over their own feet. Five stars. Would haunt again."),
("Threat Two", "Every night I climb out of the radio and stand behind one of you. Tonight? [whispers] You. [pause] Just kidding. [whispers] Or am I."),
("Fart Two", "Let me set the mood for this next song. [farts] [pause] Mood is set. Nobody speak of this. I will find you if you speak of this."),
("Lore: Hounds", "Hounds. Stupid dogs on two legs. If you stare at them, they back off. If you cry, they come running. [laughs] I cry at them all the time. They never come. Even the dogs don't like me."),
("The Story, Part Three", "For those just tuning in, I'm trying to tell my origin. I was born in the dark. My mother was the dark. My father was a broken lightbulb. [pause] That part is true, actually."),
("Cashew Water Two", "I'm thirsty again. Is this almond water? It says almond. [gulps] [coughs] [gags] [wheezing] That says CASHEW. Who wrote cashew in almond letters. [crunching] I'm eating chips now. Don't watch me."),
("Lore: Level 37", "The Poolrooms. Level thirty-seven. I went once. Lots of water, lots of light. [shudders] Horrible place. I hid in a drain for six days. Best swim of my life."),
("Lore: Partygoers", "Partygoers. That girl on the other station. Sprinkles. [growls] Everything is cake with her. You know what's in her cake? [pause] You don't want to know. Even I don't want to know."),
("Threat Three", "Ralph says don't smile back at things in the dark. [chuckles] Ralph is a smart man. Ralph should check behind his studio door tonight. [whispers] Hi Ralph."),
("Lore: Almond Water", "The humans worship almond water. It heals them, they say. It calms them. [scoffs] I drank some once. Now I'm calm. I hate being calm. Get it out of me."),
("Lore: No-clipping", "You know how most of you got here? You no-clipped. Fell through reality like a dropped sandwich. [laughs] Clumsy. I didn't fall. I was invited. By myself."),
("The Story, Part Four", "Okay. For real this time. The story of Ole'hba. In the beginning, there was the hum. And the hum said... [hum buzzes loudly] [shouting] SHUT UP, HUM. It never lets me finish."),
("Snack Break", "Snack break. [crunching loudly into the mic] [chewing] [swallows] Mmm. Don't ask what it was. It had a backpack. [chuckles]"),
("Lore: Level 0", "Level Zero. The lobby. Six hundred million square miles of wet carpet. Some of you are standing on it right now. [sniffs] I can smell you from here. Mildew and fear. My favorite."),
("Threat Four", "If you're hearing this, you're already closer to the basement than you think. [whispers] Every step down is a step toward me. [pause] Bring snacks. Not cashew."),
("Station ID 3", "This is eight bit hits. Eighty-eight point eight. Your host, Ole'hba. [farts quietly] [pause] That one was an accident. Back to the music."),
]
